Compose a canonical bead **body** for this ticket. Run the ticket description through the wiki→Markdown converter (see the jira2md helper), then wrap the JIRA-managed content between sync markers so local additions can be preserved:

```
<!-- jira-sync:begin (managed by JIRA sync — content here is overwritten on each run) -->
**JIRA:** <KEY> — <status> · <issue type> · assignee: <assignee>
**Link:** https://<jira-instance>/browse/<KEY>

<the converted ticket description (Markdown)>
<!-- jira-sync:end -->
```

**Preserve local body edits.** Take the bead's existing `description`, keep everything **after** the `<!-- jira-sync:end -->` marker verbatim, and replace only the `jira-sync:begin`…`jira-sync:end` region with the freshly composed managed block above. If the existing body has no markers (an older bead created before this convention), treat its entire current text as local content and append it **below** the new managed block so nothing is lost. Write the spliced result to a temp file, then apply the update via `bd update ... --body-file <temp>`.

Use these mappings when writing the bead:

- **Priority** (JIRA → beads): Highest→0, High→1, Medium→2, Low→3, Lowest→4 (default 2).
- **Type** (JIRA → beads): Bug→bug, Story→feature, Epic→epic, Task/Sub-task/other→task.

Always `--body-file` (never inline `--body "..."`) so Markdown survives shell quoting.
